       "title": "Retraction Radar",
       "text": "Researchers sometimes cite papers that were later retracted without knowing it. We built a command-line tool that reads a BibTeX file, checks each DOI against the public Retraction Watch database export and Crossref, and prints the retracted ones with the retraction notice. We ran it on the bibliographies of 20 open-access theses from our university: it flagged 3 real retracted citations that the authors confirmed. Stack: Python, Crossref API. Demo: run it on a sample thesis bibliography"
      }
